### Example 1: State Agency Claims Processing with Role-Based Access

**Context**: California Medicaid program has 450 claims processing staff, 35 supervisors, and 12 program administrators requiring different access levels to claims, member data, and administrative functions. Previous custom authorization code in each microservice caused inconsistent enforcement and audit difficulties.

**Requirements**:
- Claims processors can view and update claims, but cannot approve claims over $5,000
- Supervisors can approve any claim amount and view audit logs for their team
- Administrators have read-only access to all data plus user management capabilities
- All roles limited to California data only (multi-state isolation)
- Audit trail required for all PHI access per HIPAA

**Implementation**:

```yaml
# Role Definitions
CA-ClaimsProcessor:
  description: "California claims processing staff"
  permissions:
    - claims:read:state:CA
    - claims:update:state:CA
    - claims:adjudicate:state:CA
    - claims:approve:under-5000:state:CA
    - provider:read:state:CA
    - member:read:demographics:state:CA  # Limited PHI
  azure_ad_group: "GW-ClaimsProcessor-CA"
  user_count: 450

CA-ClaimsSupervisor:
  description: "California claims supervisors"
  inherits: [CA-ClaimsProcessor]
  additional_permissions:
    - claims:approve:any-amount:state:CA
    - claims:void:state:CA
    - audit_logs:view:team:state:CA
  azure_ad_group: "GW-ClaimsSupervisor-CA"
  user_count: 35

CA-StateAdmin:
  description: "California program administrators"
  permissions:
    - "*:read:state:CA"  # Read-only access to all CA data
    - reports:generate:state:CA
    - users:manage:state:CA
  azure_ad_group: "GW-StateAdmin-CA"
  user_count: 12
```

**ASP.NET Core Implementation**:

```csharp
[ApiController]
[Route("api/v1/claims")]
[Authorize] // Require authentication
public class ClaimsController : ControllerBase
{
    [HttpPost("{claimId}/approve")]
    [Authorize(Roles = "CA-ClaimsProcessor,CA-ClaimsSupervisor,CA-StateAdmin")]
    public async Task<IActionResult> ApproveClaim(
        string claimId,
        [FromBody] ClaimApprovalRequest request)
    {
        var claim = await _claimsRepo.GetClaimAsync(claimId);

        if (claim == null)
            return NotFound();

        // State isolation check
        var userState = User.FindFirst("state")?.Value;
        if (claim.ServiceState != "CA" || userState != "CA")
        {
            await _auditLog.LogAsync("UnauthorizedAccessAttempt", new {
                user = User.Identity.Name,
                claimId,
                reason = "StateMismatch",
                userState,
                claimState = claim.ServiceState
            });
            return Forbid("User not authorized for claims from other states");
        }

        // Amount-based authorization
        var userRoles = User.Claims
            .Where(c => c.Type == "roles")
            .Select(c => c.Value)
            .ToList();

        if (request.ApprovedAmount > 5000 &&
            !userRoles.Contains("CA-ClaimsSupervisor") &&
            !userRoles.Contains("CA-StateAdmin"))
        {
            await _auditLog.LogAsync("UnauthorizedAccessAttempt", new {
                user = User.Identity.Name,
                claimId,
                reason = "AmountExceedsAuthorization",
                approvedAmount = request.ApprovedAmount,
                userRoles
            });
            return Forbid("Only supervisors can approve claims over $5,000");
        }

        // Execute approval
        await _claimsRepo.ApproveClaimAsync(claimId, request.ApprovedAmount);

        await _auditLog.LogAsync("ClaimApproved", new {
            user = User.Identity.Name,
            claimId,
            approvedAmount = request.ApprovedAmount,
            userRoles
        });

        return Ok(new {
            status = "approved",
            claimId,
            approvedAmount = request.ApprovedAmount
        });
    }
}
```

**Outcomes**:
- **Authorization Consistency**: 100% of claims APIs enforce role-based authorization using the standard pattern
- **Audit Compliance**: Centralized role documentation significantly reduces SOC 2 audit preparation time
- **User Onboarding**: New claims processor onboarding streamlined to assigning a single Azure AD group
- **Security Improvement**: Penetration test found zero authorization bypass vulnerabilities following implementation
- **Performance**: Authorization checks add average 3.2ms latency (well under 10ms target)

