### Example 3: Member FHIR API with Patient Self-Access

**Context**: CMS Interoperability Rule requires payers to provide patient access APIs allowing members to retrieve their own health records. Members authenticate and access only their own data without staff intervention.

**Requirements**:
- Members authenticate via OAuth 2.0 with member ID in JWT
- Members can access only their own PHI (claims, conditions, medications, etc.)
- SMART on FHIR apps access member data with member consent
- No staff approval required (information blocking compliance)
- All member data access audited

**Implementation**:

```yaml
MemberUser:
  description: "Medicaid members accessing own health records"
  permissions:
    - member:read:own
    - claims:read:own
    - conditions:read:own
    - medications:read:own
    - immunizations:read:own
    - benefits:read:own
  data_scope_rules:
    - "resource.subject.reference = 'Patient/' + user.member_id"
  okta_group: "Members"
  user_count: 850000
```

**Java Spring Boot FHIR Endpoint**:

```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/fhir/r4")
public class FHIRPatientAccessController {

    @GetMapping("/Patient/{patientId}")
    @PreAuthorize("hasRole('MemberUser')")
    public ResponseEntity<Patient> getPatient(
            @PathVariable String patientId,
            @AuthenticationPrincipal OAuth2User principal) {

        String userMemberId = principal.getAttribute("member_id");

        // Enforce patient can only access own data
        if (!patientId.equals(userMemberId)) {
            auditService.logUnauthorizedAccess(
                principal.getName(),
                "Patient",
                patientId,
                "MemberIdMismatch"
            );

            return ResponseEntity
                .status(HttpStatus.FORBIDDEN)
                .body(null);
        }

        Patient patient = fhirService.getPatient(patientId);

        auditService.logFHIRAccess(
            principal.getName(),
            "Patient",
            patientId,
            "read"
        );

        return ResponseEntity.ok(patient);
    }

    @GetMapping("/Claim")
    @PreAuthorize("hasRole('MemberUser')")
    public ResponseEntity<Bundle> getClaims(
            @RequestParam(required = false) String patient,
            @AuthenticationPrincipal OAuth2User principal) {

        String userMemberId = principal.getAttribute("member_id");

        // If patient parameter provided, verify it matches authenticated member
        if (patient != null && !patient.equals("Patient/" + userMemberId)) {
            return ResponseEntity
                .status(HttpStatus.FORBIDDEN)
                .body(null);
        }

        // Force patient filter to authenticated member
        Bundle claims = fhirService.getClaims(
            "Patient/" + userMemberId
        );

        auditService.logFHIRAccess(
            principal.getName(),
            "Claim",
            null,
            "search"
        );

        return ResponseEntity.ok(claims);
    }
}
```

**Outcomes**:
- **CMS Compliance**: 100% of members can access own health records without staff approval (information blocking compliance)
- **Patient Empowerment**: Members can self-serve access to their own health records via the patient access API
- **Zero Unauthorized Access**: Members cannot access other members' data (enforced via member ID matching)
- **SMART App Ecosystem**: Third-party SMART on FHIR apps integrated for medication management, appointment scheduling, care coordination
